Find the coterminal angle to \(\frac{27 \pi}{5}\) over the interval \(\left[-360^{\circ}, 0^{\circ}\right)\).

\section*{Solution}

Method 1
\[
\begin{aligned}
\frac{27 \pi}{5}\left(\frac{180^{\circ}}{\pi}\right) & =27\left(36^{\circ}\right) \\
& =972^{\circ} \\
972^{\circ}-\left(360^{\circ}\right)(3) & =-108^{\circ}
\end{aligned}
\]

1 mark for conversion to degrees
\(\frac{1}{2}\) mark for coterminal angle \(\frac{1}{2}\) mark for correct domain

2 marks

Method 2
\[
\begin{aligned}
& -\frac{3 \pi}{5} \text { is a coterminal angle to } \frac{27 \pi}{5} \\
& -\frac{3 \pi}{5} \cdot \frac{180^{\circ}}{\pi}=-108^{\circ}
\end{aligned}
\]
\(\frac{1}{2}\) mark for coterminal angle \(\frac{1}{2}\) mark for correct domain

1 mark for conversion to degrees
