\section*{Solution}

Method 1
\[
\begin{aligned}
\log _{a} 9 & =1.129 \\
\log _{a} 3^{2} & =1.129 \\
2 \log _{a} 3 & =1.129 \\
\log _{a} 3 & =0.5645
\end{aligned}
\]

1 mark for power rule
\[
\begin{aligned}
\log _{a} 12 & =\log _{a}(4 \cdot 3) \\
& =\log _{a} 4+\log _{a} 3 \\
& =0.712+0.5645 \\
& =1.2765 \\
& =1.277
\end{aligned}
\]

1 mark for writing 12 as a product
1 mark for product rule
3 marks

